- **Ensure color consistency**: You’re already setting the background color of the dropdown to `#3d3d3d`, which should match the navbar. This will create a seamless look when the dropdown is open.
- **Dropdown Item Padding**: You might want to adjust the padding of dropdown items to ensure they have proper spacing that looks good without introducing unwanted margins that could create gaps.

### Testing

After making these adjustments, be sure to test the dropdown in various browsers and screen sizes to confirm that the changes work as expected. If you still see inconsistencies, additional debugging with browser developer tools can help identify any remaining margins or padding that may not be overridden.

